      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking a higher dose of lisinopril without medical guidance is risky and could lead to a severe drop in blood pressure, which is not what you want before a drive. Your body adjusts to medication gradually, and rushing this process with extra doses is dangerous. If the dizziness is significantly impacting your ability to function, you must call your doctor or a pharmacist for safe advice before your drive tomorrow.",
      "source": "target",
